    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/casual-collection-assistant-cairns-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Casual Collection Assistant",
      "description": "Casual Collection Assistant - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Casual Collection Assistant 495783 Cairns Professional Casual Closing on: Sep 11 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Are you a current JCU student looking for flexible, on-campus work? Join the Cairns Library team and help create an organised, welcoming and accessible learning environment for fellow students and staff. Casual opportunity based at JCU's Cairns Nguma-bada Campus Approximately 4-6 hours per week Flexible hours to fit around your studies Training and support provided WHAT YOU CAN ACCOMPLISH IN THE ROLE As a Collection Assistant, you'll play an important role in maintaining the Library's collections and study spaces, ensuring resources are easy to find and accessible for the JCU community. Shelve books and journals accurately and maintain collection order. Conduct shelf checks and collection audits to support collection management projects. Retrieve, scan and assist with the repair of library materials. Support collection relocation and maintenance activities. Help maintain a clean, organised and welcoming library environment. Identify and report maintenance issues and space constraints. Provide basic directional assistance and referrals to library users when required. WHAT YOU CAN BRING TO THE ROLE To be successful, you'll have: Current enrolment as a JCU student based in Cairns. Strong attention to detail and organisational skills. A reliable and proactive approach to work. Good communication and customer service skills. The ability to work independently and as part of a team. HOW TO APPLY Submit your current resume and a short statement outlining your interest in the role and your availability. Applicants must be current JCU students located in Cairns to be eligible for this opportunity. Recommended for you Project Officer Townsville Professional Be part of delivering impactful infrastructure projects 