    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/team-leader-hdr-program-support-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Team Leader, HDR Program Support",
      "description": "Team Leader, HDR Program Support - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Team Leader, HDR Program Support 495219 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 13 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Full time - 36.25 hours per week | Continuing position HEWL 7 $99,878 - $110,446 + 17% super and great benefits Based in Townsville Help shape the future of research at JCU. We’re looking for a dynamic and motivated Team Leader to guide our HDR Program Support Team and deliver exceptional services to Higher Degree Research candidates and supervisors across the University. In this pivotal role, you’ll lead a small, high-performing team responsible for providing efficient, accurate and consistent academic and administrative support. You’ll coordinate workloads and priorities, streamline processes, and act as a key escalation point for complex queries—ensuring our HDR community receives outstanding service at every step. You’ll contribute to strategic planning within the Graduate Research School, drive continuous improvement initiatives, and support compliance, reporting and audit requirements through high-quality data analysis and documentation. Your ability to build strong relationships, influence stakeholders and lead with authenticity will be central to your success. What you’ll bring A relevant degree or equivalent experience in academic or research administration. Proven leadership capability, with experience developing teams and fostering a culture of service excellence. Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities and complex projects. Excellent written communication and analytical skills, with confidence preparing reports and procedural documentation. Advanced interpersonal and negotiation skills, with the ability to work effectively across diverse areas of the University. Strong problem‑solving skills and sound judgement in resolving complex operational issues. Confidence using enterprise systems, databases and digital tools to support workflow efficiency. Join a university committed to excellence, sustainability, reconciliation and delivering a brighter future for the Tropics. If you’re passionate about leading people, improving processes and supporting research success, we’d love to hear from you. How to Apply and Contact Details Apply now and help empower the next generation of researchers at JCU. Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and how your skills align with the role Applications close: 14 September 2025 For further information, contact Gabby Ryan via email gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all. We encourage applications from people of all backgrounds who meet the role requirements. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 2ecbca6a Last Name (required) f2681fe4 Email (required) b3798fac Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Project Officer Townsville Professional Be part of delivering impactful infrastructure projects across diverse locations, where you’ll provide high-level administrative support, coordinate key activities, ensure financial accuracy, mitigate contract risks, and champion continuous improvements. Finance Officer Townsville Professional Bring your finance expertise to a role where accuracy meets impact, helping deliver trusted financial insights, outstanding customer service and accurate reporting across one of Australia's leading tropical universities. Student Finance Officer Townsville Professional Join JCU's Student Finance team in a fixed-term opportunity until 2 March 2028. Use your financial administration experience in a role that combines compliance, problem-solving and customer service while supporting scholarship, bursary and grant programs and delivering accurate student finance services. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 68002db8 Last Name (required) b586d1be Email (required) 2af80b20 Job Alert 25006e61 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Graduate Research School Graduate Research School Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
