    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-senior-lecturer-social-work-cairns-qld-australia-townsville": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Social Work",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Social Work - Cairns, QLD, Australia - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Social Work 495676 Cairns Townsville Academic Full time Closing on: Sep 27 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Full time - 36.25 hours per week | Continuing Appointment Academic Level B - $112,810 - $133,110 Academic Level C - $137,166 - $157,465 17% Super, 5 weeks annual leave, leave loading & other great benefits Can be based in either Cairns or Townsville Are you passionate about shaping the future of Social Work in the Tropics? James Cook University is seeking an inspiring academic to join our Social Work team and contribute to high‑quality teaching, impactful research, and meaningful community engagement across Northern Queensland. As a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer, you’ll play a key role in developing and delivering innovative curriculum across our Social Work and Human Services programs, including the Bachelor of Social Work, Bachelor of Human Services, and Master of Social Work (Professional Qualifying). You’ll help create inclusive, student‑centred learning experiences that prepare graduates for contemporary practice in diverse communities. You will also contribute to JCU’s research strengths by producing high‑quality publications, pursuing external funding opportunities, and supervising Higher Degree Research candidates. Your work will support strong partnerships with community agencies, field education providers, and professional bodies, helping to enhance placement opportunities and strengthen JCU’s presence across the region. This is an opportunity to join a collegial, supportive team committed to excellence in teaching, research, and community impact—aligned with JCU’s Strategic Intent and our commitment to reconciliation, sustainability, and equity. What you’ll bring A PhD (or pathway to completion) in Social Work, Human Services or a related discipline. Successful experience teaching Social Work or cognate programs using contemporary, inclusive pedagogies across online, blended and face‑to‑face modes. A developing or established research profile with ERA‑recognised publications and a clear research agenda. Experience contributing to field education learning and supporting students on placement. Strong collaboration skills and the ability to work effectively within teaching, research and community engagement teams. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the capacity to represent JCU’s Social Work programs externally. Why Join JCU? Join a university that’s deeply connected to its community and committed to improving health outcomes in rural, remote, and underserved regions. At JCU, you’ll be part of a vibrant academic environment that values diversity, equity, and sustainability.  We offer: 5 weeks annual leave + leave loading Flexible working arrangements Up to 6 months paid parental leave Salary packaging options Staff study assistance & paid study leave Fitness Passport & health insurance discounts Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching & counselling) Ongoing professional development support How to Apply and Contact Details If you’re ready to make a meaningful contribution to Social Work education and research in a region where your work truly matters, we’d love to hear from you. Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and how your skills align with the role For further information, contact Professor Lucy Jordan on 4232 1276  or via email lucy.jordan@jcu.edu.au Apply now and help shape the next generation of Social Workers in the Tropics. JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all. We encourage applications from people of all backgrounds who meet the role requirements. Recommended for you Project Officer Townsville Professional Be part of delivering impactful infrastructure projects across diverse locations, where you’ll provide high-level administrative support, coordinate key activities, ensure financial accuracy, mitigate contract risks, and champion continuous improvements. Finance Officer Townsville Professional Bring your finance expertise to a role where accuracy meets impact, helping deliver trusted financial insights, outstanding customer service and accurate reporting across one of Australia's leading tropical universities. Student Finance Officer Townsville Professional Join JCU's Student Finance team in a fixed-term opportunity until 2 March 2028. Use your financial administration experience in a role that combines compliance, problem-solving and customer service while supporting scholarship, bursary and grant programs and delivering accurate student finance services. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
