    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/research-training-and-researcher-development-advisor-townsville-qld-australia-a2be3fde-e948-471e-8b60-151887273448": {
      "title": "Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor",
      "description": "Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor 495426 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 13 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description 12-month fixed-term contract Full-time – 36.25 hours per week HEWL 8 – $111,960 – $128,567 + 17% superannuation and great benefits Based in Townsville – applicants must be currently based in Townsville Current JCU students are not eligible to apply At James Cook University (JCU) , we are committed to creating a brighter future for the people of Northern Australia and the Tropics worldwide. As Australia’s leading tropical university, our research tackles some of the world’s most pressing challenges and creates meaningful impact for communities locally and globally. We are seeking an enthusiastic and innovative Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor to join the Graduate Research School within the Research Division. In this rewarding role, you'll play a pivotal part in enhancing the experience of Higher Degree by Research (HDR) candidates, researchers and research support staff through engaging research training and researcher development initiatives. Why you'll love this role This is an opportunity to make a real difference to JCU's research community. You'll design and deliver impactful learning experiences, foster meaningful connections across the University, and help develop the skills and capabilities of emerging and established researchers. You'll join a highly collaborative environment where creativity, innovation and continuous improvement are valued, working alongside passionate colleagues dedicated to research excellence. What you'll be doing As the Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor , you will: Design and deliver contemporary research training and researcher development programs across multiple campuses and online platforms. Create engaging learning materials and content that maximise participant engagement and learning outcomes. Build strong partnerships across the University and with external stakeholders to source expert presenters and facilitators. Evaluate program effectiveness, analyse feedback and outcomes, and identify opportunities for continuous improvement. Collaborate across the University to strengthen pathways into Higher Degree by Research programs and support successful research outcomes. Contribute to the strategic objectives and success of the Graduate Research School, Research Division and the broader University. What you'll bring We're looking for someone who is passionate about learning, community building and supporting researcher success. You will demonstrate: Experience working within a university or research-focused environment and an understanding of the needs of researchers and research students. Outstanding communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage diverse stakeholders. Experience developing networks, fostering community engagement and coordinating events, workshops or professional development activities. Strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities, with a focus on continuous improvement and innovation. Excellent written and digital communication skills, including developing engaging online content and learning resources. Why James Cook University? At JCU, our people are at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to developing the skills, knowledge and capability of our staff while fostering a culture of respect, excellence and sustainability. When you join JCU, you'll become part of a university that is: Driven by purpose and impact. Committed to research excellence and innovation. Focused on creating opportunities for growth and professional development. Guided by the values of Excellence, Authenticity, Integrity and Respect . You'll enjoy: A collaborative and supportive team environment. Flexible work arrangements where operationally appropriate. Generous superannuation and leave entitlements. Professional development opportunities. Ready to make a difference? If you're excited about empowering researchers, building vibrant learning communities and contributing to world-class research outcomes, we'd love to hear from you. please note that this position is based in Townsville and applicants must be currently based in Townsville. Current JCU students are not eligible to apply for this position. Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the online application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your experience and how your skills align with the role. For more information, please contact Gabby Ryan via email at gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au . Recommended for you Project Officer Townsville Professional Be part of delivering impactful infrastructure projects across diverse locations, where you’ll provide high-level administrative support, coordinate key activities, ensure financial accuracy, mitigate contract risks, and champion continuous improvements. Finance Officer Townsville Professional Bring your finance expertise to a role where accuracy meets impact, helping deliver trusted financial insights, outstanding customer service and accurate reporting across one of Australia's leading tropical universities. Student Finance Officer Townsville Professional Join JCU's Student Finance team in a fixed-term opportunity until 2 March 2028. Use your financial administration experience in a role that combines compliance, problem-solving and customer service while supporting scholarship, bursary and grant programs and delivering accurate student finance services. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
