    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/educational-designer-cairns-qld-australia-townsville": {
      "title": "Educational Designer",
      "description": "Educational Designer - Cairns, QLD, Australia - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Educational Designer 495694 Cairns Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Sep 13 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally, James Cook University (JCU) is seeking an innovative and collaborative Educational Designer to join our team. Full-time, continuing position Located at either the Townsville Bebegu Yumba, Cairns Nguma-bada campus or Remote Academic Level B (plus up to 17% employer superannuation contributions, leave loading and other generous employee benefits) WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You are an experienced educational design professional with a passion for enhancing learning and teaching through innovative, inclusive and technology-enhanced educational practices. You thrive in collaborative environments and have a demonstrated ability to partner with educators and stakeholders to co-design and co-develop engaging curriculum, learning experiences and assessment that support student success. Drawing on your expertise in curriculum development, pedagogy, assessment design, learning technology integration and evidence-informed decision making, you provide high-level advice and support to educators to create impactful learning experiences for diverse learners across a range of disciplines and delivery modes. You will bring extensive experience in learning design, contemporary educational technologies and inclusive teaching practices, with the ability to apply evidence-based approaches and Universal Design for Learning (UDL) principles to improve curriculum quality and student outcomes. Your project management capability, scholarly mindset and collaborative approach will enable you to lead complex curriculum and assessment initiatives while contributing to JCU's learning and teaching scholarship. With exceptional communication and stakeholder engagement skills, you will build productive partnerships across the University and play a key role in advancing innovative educational practices that support JCU's strategic learning and teaching priorities. WHAT YOU CAN ACCOMPLISH IN THE ROLE Partner with educators and stakeholders to co-design and develop inclusive, student-centred curriculum, learning activities and assessment aligned with JCU's learning and teaching priorities. Apply contemporary pedagogical expertise, evidence-based design principles and innovative technologies to create engaging learning experiences across a variety of disciplines and learning modes. Lead and manage curriculum, assessment and course design projects, working collaboratively within multidisciplinary teams to deliver strategic educational outcomes. Design and facilitate professional learning opportunities that build educator capability in the effective use of learning technologies, digital resources and innovative teaching practices. Enhance the student learning experience through data-informed approaches, learning analytics and the application of emerging technologies that support engagement, accessibility and success. Provide expert advice and guidance on inclusive learning design, curriculum enhancement, assessment practice and technology integration. Contribute to the scholarship of learning and teaching through research, publication and dissemination of innovative educational practice. Support the development of institutional policies, frameworks and initiatives that advance JCU's strategic goals for learning and teaching excellence. It is a requirement of this position to undertake travel and/or attend conferences deemed necessary to the advancement and success of learning and teaching at James Cook University. WHY JCU? JCU offers a culturally diverse working environment with opportunities for professional and personal growth. Employee wellbeing is at the core of our values, and we support our people through a range of benefits, including: Up to 17% employer superannuation contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks annual recreation leave 15 days paid sick/personal/carer's leave per year Flexible working options Salary packaging opportunities Fitness Passport Employee Assistance Program Professional development opportunities Staff study assistance Health insurance discounts Access to campus facilities including medical services, cafés, gyms and childcare HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page, create an applicant account and follow the steps below: 1.            Complete the application form 2.            Upload your current resume 3.            Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success. Applications close Sunday, 13th September at 11.55pm. ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 178d4f9a Last Name (required) 278c51dd Email (required) 19e6a5c6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Project Officer Townsville Professional Be part of delivering impactful infrastructure projects across diverse locations, where you’ll provide high-level administrative support, coordinate key activities, ensure financial accuracy, mitigate contract risks, and champion continuous improvements. Finance Officer Townsville Professional Bring your finance expertise to a role where accuracy meets impact, helping deliver trusted financial insights, outstanding customer service and accurate reporting across one of Australia's leading tropical universities. Student Finance Officer Townsville Professional Join JCU's Student Finance team in a fixed-term opportunity until 2 March 2028. Use your financial administration experience in a role that combines compliance, problem-solving and customer service while supporting scholarship, bursary and grant programs and delivering accurate student finance services. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) d1ba8a74 Last Name (required) 6bb3671e Email (required) 94c8adbe Job Alert 01e0391c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Education Design, Quality & Standards Education Design, Quality & Standards Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Cairns, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Cairns, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
