    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/casual-nursing-technical-support-mackay-mackay-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Casual Nursing Technical Support",
      "description": "Casual Nursing Technical Support - Mackay - Mackay, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Casual Nursing Technical Support - Mackay 495122 Mackay Professional Casual Closing on: Sep 25 2026 Add to favourites View favourites About Nursing at JCU James Cook University (JCU) Nursing is recognised as a leader in regional, rural and tropical healthcare education. Our programs foster a vibrant and supportive learning culture that develops highly skilled, knowledgeable and compassionate graduates. Through authentic, hands-on learning experiences, we empower students with the confidence and capability to become effective healthcare professionals. We are inviting Expressions of Interest from suitably experienced and motivated technical professionals to join the Laboratory & Technical Support unit on a casual basis in Mackay. About the Opportunity Based at our purpose-built clinical teaching facilities in Mackay, you will support the practical delivery of high-quality nursing education through: Supporting technical service delivery and equipment for undergraduate practical classes, intensives and skills sessions Preparing and maintaining stock levels, ensuring consumables and teaching resources are readily available to meet timetable requirements Maintain equipment and simulation facilities, ensuring all activities are delivered in accordance with established procedures and safety and hygiene legislation. Contributing to a safe, organised and effective practical learning environment About You To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: Technical experience with clinical and simulation laboratories, relevant to health professional education and training. Demonstrated understanding of WHS legislation and its practical application within a laboratory. Informed analytical and problem-solving skills to judge shifting priorities and conflicting deadlines, taking corrective action. Strong organisational and communication skills, with the ability to work both independently and as a member of a team in a high-volume environment Effective computer and data entry skills using the Microsoft Office suite and ability to adapt to the use of new software packages with high attention to detail. Ability to meet manual handling demands and work flexibly Why Join JCU? At JCU, we value our people and are committed to fostering a supportive, inclusive and collaborative work environment aligned with our values of respect, excellence and sustainability. Casual staff benefit from: Opportunities to contribute to meaningful education outcomes Access to professional development opportunities About North Queensland Mackay offers a relaxed tropical lifestyle complemented by modern amenities. With year-round sunshine, access to natural attractions and a strong sense of community, North Queensland provides an exceptional lifestyle and work environment. How to Submit an Expression of Interest Please submit your EOI including: A current resume A brief cover statement outlining your technical experience and interest in the role. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 7522be80 Last Name (required) 8046074f Email (required) 3e911c9d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Project Officer Townsville Professional Be part of delivering impactful infrastructure projects across diverse locations, where you’ll provide high-level administrative support, coordinate key activities, ensure financial accuracy, mitigate contract risks, and champion continuous improvements. Finance Officer Townsville Professional Bring your finance expertise to a role where accuracy meets impact, helping deliver trusted financial insights, outstanding customer service and accurate reporting across one of Australia's leading tropical universities. Student Finance Officer Townsville Professional Join JCU's Student Finance team in a fixed-term opportunity until 2 March 2028. Use your financial administration experience in a role that combines compliance, problem-solving and customer service while supporting scholarship, bursary and grant programs and delivering accurate student finance services. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) b5ca72d2 Last Name (required) b51fc6c5 Email (required) 01586d7c Job Alert 812dff32 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Academic Services Academic Services Employment Type Casual Casual Locations Mackay, QLD, Australia Mackay, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    }
